//! - `threadgroup-cap-halving-with-order-preserving-sum` (category D —
//!   candidate 4): simd_qmm.zig:429-432,553-580,688 — on a threadgroup-size
//!   cap error, halve the simdgroups and memoize per (n,k,bits,rt); bit-safe
//!   only because the chunks walked sum in the same order (same-bits test).
//! - `canary-admission-per-config-bit-equal-stock` (category D — candidate 5):
//!   gather_qmm_nax.zig:237-355 — synthetic-workload bit-compare vs stock,
//!   cached per config key, disable-with-log; the oracle is REGIME-KEYED
//!   (stock's own K-tail bug -> fp32-dequant oracle, 1/64-of-peak bar);
//!   error-latch hygiene drops only the latch the canary raised.
//! - `prompt-form-refused-toolchain-format-gap-reopen-trigger` (category D —
//!   candidate 6): qmv_nax2.zig:326-347 — the 0.87-0.93x prompt-form negative
//!   ships as an admission refusal naming the missing `uint2b_format`
//!   capability and 'Re-test if `uint2b_format` ever appears.'
//! - `per-generation-plan-table-unmeasured-generation-fallback` (category K —
//!   candidate 7): qmv2.zig:206-235 — the plan table keys on GPU generation;
//!   'a generation nobody measured keeps `legacy`' by an explicit membership
//!   test, never an extrapolated rung.
//! - `quad-lane-line-load-shuffle-word-exchange-ring` (category A — candidate
